%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: YuriinMarkarth
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335443
    - rid: 4972360342771335444
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: ... this strange cube.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335445
    - rid: 4972360342771335446
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah, a Dwarven Lexicon Cube.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335449
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: From my understanding, the Dwemer used them to store vast quantities
      of information.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: How this information is stored exactly remains a mystery- allegedly some
      sort of machine was designed for that purpose.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: What is known, is that when information is contained in the cube, it
      will display strange blue markings- which are absent from this example.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Which room did you find this in?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: I found it in the Armory chamber; one of the gates was already unlocked,
      so I could go in to grab it.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335455
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: The Armory, hm? That's curious...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335456
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: If the lexicon had data stored on it, perhaps it stored blueprints or
      instructions to create weaponry, or temper the dwemer metal-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: But no...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Calcelmo writes something down in a journal.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: This mystery has too many missing pieces to solve.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, and good work.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Do you have any questions about what you found?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335457
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: W-what were those strange, pale deformed... creatures? People?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335458
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Hm. It sounds like you encountered the Falmer.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335459
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Wait, those were the Falmer?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335460
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Like the ones that committed the Night of Tears at Saarthal?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Yes, the very same!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335461
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, it's highly unlikely that the Falmer you found were the ones that
      committed the Night of Tears specifically...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335462
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: But, the Falmer have found their home underground for centuries now;
      the consequence of the invading Nords pushing the Falmer into seeking asylum
      with the Dwemer.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Uh, w-why are they so...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335464
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Monstrous? Feral?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360342771335465
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: That would be thanks to the Dwemer.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: 'When the Dwemer took in the Falmer, they did so under one condition:'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: That the Falmer would eat a certain species of mushroom.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: To the Falmer, who didn't know about the mushroom's particular properties,
      this was an easy price to pay.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: That mushroom was incredibly toxic, causing the Falmer who ate it to
      gradually go blind.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: We're still not sure <i>why</i> the Dwemer did this; we do know that
      the Falmer served the Dwemer as servants and slaves-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: But surely a blind slave would provide less value than one that can see,
      no?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Personally, I believe the simplest explanation: the Dwemer wanted to
      guarantee that their servant population would never leave or try to rebel against
      their rule.'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360366678081682
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: But there are some other, more fringe theories; like that the Falmer
      were blinded so that their sense of hearing could be amplified-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360366678081683
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: So that they would be more in-tune to the Tonal Architecture that was
      the backbone of Dwemer innovations and society.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Of course, this is merely conjecture- as is often the case with theories
      about the Dwemer.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, the next thing I need your help with is-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: (A Thalmor-?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360390599770201
    - rid: 4972360390599770202
    - rid: 4972360390599770203
    - rid: 4972360390599770204
    - rid: 4972360390599770205
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: O-Ondolemar, do you need something?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360390599770206
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: Hm. New apprentice?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: That's right, I figured I'd finally grant my nephew's wish-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: You. What's your name?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: M-m-me?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360390599770207
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: M-my name is Y-Yuri...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360390599770208
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: Hm? You have no reason to be scared of me-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360390599770209
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: Unless there's something you are better off confessing now?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360390599770210
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: N-n-no...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360390599770211
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: ... very well.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: Calcelmo, where did you find this nervous wreck?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: She said she came from Winterhold-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: Winterhold...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: Well then, Yuri, you wouldn't know what happened to Ancano, would you?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360390599770212
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm sure you've seen him around; he's our ambassador to your college.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: I ask because Elenwyn hasn't received any communications from him recently.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: H-he... uhh...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360390599770213
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: He? He what? Spit it out, girl.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360390599770215
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: H-he died...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446656
    - rid: 4972360411925446657
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446658
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: And your college did not immediately report this?!?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446659
    - rid: 4972360411925446660
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7d80eed2ca09b7d47be584961af25467, type: 2}
    dialog: I assure you, your college <i>will</i> answer for this transgression.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Ondolemar storms off in a huff.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446661
    - rid: 4972360411925446662
    - rid: 4972360411925446663
    - rid: 4972360411925446664
    - rid: 4972360411925446665
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: ... What was that about?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446666
    - rid: 4972360411925446667
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Yuri recounts Ancano''s story for Calcelmo:'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446668
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Finding the Eye of Magnus, Ancano manipulating it, and using the Staff
      of Magnus to defeat him.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: That Eye was powerful enough for the Psijics to get involved?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446669
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: We have to consider ourselves lucky that Ancano wasn't versed enough
      in the arcane to do any major damage.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446670
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: I assume that you'll want to return to your college for the duration
      of this Thalmor situation?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446671
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Um, no, I wasn't really thinking about that-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446672
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh! That actually reminds me...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446673
    - rid: 4972360411925446675
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: You wouldn't happen to have any filled soul gems on you?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446676
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Souls gems? Are you planning on doing some enchanting?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446674
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: That's right, I'd like to enchant some sort of curio to contain a mark
      spell.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446677
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: A mark? How do you know about that spell-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446678
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: 'It fell heavily out of favor after the Third era, when the Mages'' Guild
      banned it in Imperial territory. '
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: The mark spell was banned? Why?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446679
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8c9256f0136990746a31b7a644716f46, type: 2}
    dialog: Probably the same reason the levitation spell was banned by the guild-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360411925446680
